ateret_zekenim.en:
(א) Permitted to marry a woman on Purim. {Rama: And some say one may not marry on Purim, neither on the 14th nor on the 15th, so as not to mix his joy with Purim joy (Mordechai and Beit Diniya in responsum of Mahari Weil in Hagahah).}<br>
<br>
(ב) And likewise wearing shaatnez, which is d'rabbanan. {Rama: There too it is good to be stringent and serve God with joy and to be joyful with trembling.}
